From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 23:30:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] BISECT: revert XD graphics to v0.4.28 to test the
 solo-detection regression

Throwaway test patch. v0.4.28 solo detected the GBA; v0.4.30 does not, and
cheats (patch 71) is ruled out by an on-device toggle test. Patch 73's reset
path is verified unchanged. This reverts patch 72's graphics preset to the
v0.4.28 values to confirm whether the graphics change is what broke detection.
If solo detection works with this build, the graphics preset is the cause.
---
 Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini | 16 ++++------------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini b/Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini
index f0e9c182ad..bd631a3066 100644
--- a/Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini
+++ b/Data/Sys/GameSettings/GXXE01.ini
@@ -44,15 +44,7 @@ $16:9 Widescreen
 $60 FPS
 
 [Video_Settings]
-# Stability preset for Adreno (AYN Thor). The GameCube renders on the top
-# screen via Vulkan; ubershaders (ShaderCompilationMode = 2) produce GPU
-# submissions long enough to trip Adreno's watchdog when a new move/effect
-# first appears mid-battle -> VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST, which Dolphin cannot
-# recover from (the top screen freezes for the session). Specialized
-# shaders + pre-warming the cache avoid that entirely; native resolution
-# and CPU-side culling give thermal/submission headroom. None of these
-# affect netplay determinism.
-ShaderCompilationMode = 0
-WaitForShadersBeforeStarting = True
-InternalResolution = 1
-CPUCull = True
\ No newline at end of file
+# BISECT TEST: graphics reverted to v0.4.28 values to check if patch 72
+# broke GBA detection. (Ubershaders/2x -- reintroduces the GPU crash; test only.)
+InternalResolution = 2
+ShaderCompilationMode = 2
